Author: telecomadm1145 <47657299+telecomadm1145@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri May 15 23:34:42 2026 +0800

    🛡️ Sentinel: [CRITICAL] Fix command injection in SysDialog.cpp (#40)
    
    This commit fixes a critical command injection vulnerability in the `SystemDialogs::SaveFileDialog` method. Previously, the user-provided `preferred_name` was directly concatenated into the shell commands for `zenity` and `kdialog`. Now, `preferred_name` is safely escaped using a new `escape_shell_arg` function before being used.
    
    Co-authored-by: google-labs-jules[bot] <161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

[33mcommit 9b1b846e2434705a5d17888b32af0cf9905d9a97[m
Author: telecomadm1145 <47657299+telecomadm1145@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed May 6 01:43:34 2026 +0800

    Avoid std::string allocations in Localization lookup (#38)
    
    This commit eliminates implicit `std::string` heap allocations in the
    `Localization::Get()` and `Localization::GetCStr()` methods by defining a
    transparent `StringHash` struct with `is_transparent = void`. This enables C++20
    heterogeneous lookup on `std::unordered_map`, avoiding costly allocations when
    looking up string constants. This lookup occurs heavily during the ImGui UI
    render loop through the `_lc` operator.
    
    Co-authored-by: google-labs-jules[bot] <161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

