[33mcommit c0f52fd2a8512043adc59a3330fd01b4982d43e2[m
Author: telecomadm1145 <47657299+telecomadm1145@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat May 2 02:31:34 2026 +0800

    Fix crash when raising invalid maskable interrupt in HwController (#36)
    
    This change modifies `CasioEmuMsvc/Gui/HwController.cpp` to validate the interrupt index before calling `m_emu->chipset.RaiseMaskable(irq)`.
    
    - Initializes `irq` to 5 (the lowest valid maskable interrupt index) instead of 0.
    - Adds a bounds check to ensure `irq` is between 5 and 63 (inclusive of 5, exclusive of 64).
    
    This prevents the application from hitting the `PANIC` macro and crashing with `EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT` when the user triggers an interrupt with an invalid index via the debug UI.
    
    Co-authored-by: google-labs-jules[bot] <161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

