    Merge pull request #26 from telecomadm1145/fix-injector-crash-race-condition-13657443328949502331
    
    Fix Access Violation in Injector::BackgroundReload due to race condition

[33mcommit 9b5208bf87850b6308899efbb633078b15f511b8[m
Author: google-labs-jules[bot] <161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Feb 7 18:00:03 2026 +0000

    Fix Access Violation in Injector::BackgroundReload by managing thread lifecycle
    
    - Added `std::thread reloadThread` to `Injector` class to manage the background reloading thread.
    - Updated `Injector::~Injector` to join `reloadThread` instead of sleeping, ensuring the thread finishes before the object is destroyed.
    - Updated `Injector::AsyncLoadCustomInjections` to use `reloadThread` and join any existing thread before starting a new one.
    - Updated `RenderCustomInjectTab` and `RenderCore` to use `AsyncLoadCustomInjections` for consistent thread management.
    - Fixed a race condition where `Injector` object destruction could occur while `BackgroundReload` was still running, leading to a crash when accessing `injectionMutex`.
    
    Co-authored-by: telecomadm1145 <47657299+telecomadm1145@users.noreply.github.com>

